DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccll__ccaallcc__mmaasskk() function is a POSIX.1e call that calculates and set
     the permissions associated with the ACL_MASK ACL entry of the ACL re‐
     ferred to by _a_c_l___p.

     The value of new permissions are the union of the permissions granted by
     the ACL_GROUP, ACL_GROUP_OBJ, ACL_USER tag types which match processes in
     the file group class contained in the ACL referred to by _a_c_l___p.

     If the ACL referred to by _a_c_l___p already contains an ACL_MASK entry, its
     permissions shall be overwritten; if it does not contain an ACL_MASK en‐
     try, one shall be added.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The aaccll__ccaallcc__mmaasskk() function returns the value 0 if successful; otherwise
     the value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate
     the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The aaccll__ccaallcc__mmaasskk() function fails if:

     [EINVAL]           Argument _a_c_l___p does not point to a pointer to a valid
                        ACL.

